IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- LAYER 1, MODULE 4: REGULATION 2(2)
-- (couples and polygamous marriages: the enhanced rate for only the elder or eldest
-- of the children) AND REGULATION 2(3) (what a polygamous marriage is).
--
-- Paragraph (2)(b) is "child benefit would, but for this paragraph, be payable to
-- that person ... at the enhanced rate": that is the result of paragraphs (1)(a), (4)
-- and (5), which cbr-reg2-rate works out and passes in here as a plain BOOLEAN, so
-- that this module does not import the module that imports it.
--
-- NOT COVERED, returned as NOTHING (never FALSE): two children born on the same day,
-- where the text does not say which is "the elder" (fork F3).

§ `Regulation 2(2) and (3): couples and polygamous marriages`

§§ `Regulation 2(3): a member of a polygamous marriage`

-- src:29 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a) a person is a member of a polygamous marriage if—
-- src:30 | (a) during the subsistence of the marriage any party to it is married to more than one person; and
-- src:31 | (b) the ceremony of marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy.
@ref reg 2(3) (src:29-31)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` claimant MEANS
        claimant's `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person`                          -- (a)
    AND claimant's `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`    -- (b)

§§ `Regulation 2(2)(a): the persons the paragraph is about`

-- src:21 | (2) If, in any week—
-- src:22 | (a) a person is—
-- src:23 | (i) living with his spouse or civil partner,
-- src:24 | (ii) living with another person as his spouse or civil partner, or
-- src:25 | (iii) a member of a polygamous marriage and is residing with other members of that marriage;
@ref reg 2(2)(a) (src:21-25)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` claimant MEANS
        claimant's `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner`                      -- (i)
    OR  claimant's `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner`    -- (ii)
    OR  (   `a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` claimant                       -- (iii)
        AND claimant's `residing with other members of that marriage`)

§§ `Regulation 2(2): only the elder or eldest of the children keeps the enhanced rate`

-- "the elder or eldest": the child born earlier is the elder. Two children born on
-- the same day: the text does not say which is the elder, so NOTHING (fork F3).
-- src:28 | the enhanced rate shall be payable in that week in respect of only the elder or eldest of the children and qualifying young persons referred to in sub-paragraphs (b) and (c).
@ref reg 2(2), closing words (src:28)
GIVEN `date of birth of the claimant's child` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the elder or eldest of the other children` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` `date of birth of the claimant's child` `date of birth of the elder or eldest of the other children` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date of birth of the claimant's child` LESS THAN `date of birth of the elder or eldest of the other children` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `date of birth of the claimant's child` GREATER THAN `date of birth of the elder or eldest of the other children` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- JUST TRUE: paragraph (2) leaves the enhanced rate for this child (either it does
-- not apply, or the child is the elder or eldest). JUST FALSE: the enhanced rate is
-- payable only for an older child of another person, so not for this child.
-- NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- src:21 | (2) If, in any week—
-- src:22 | (a) a person is—
-- src:23 | (i) living with his spouse or civil partner,
-- src:24 | (ii) living with another person as his spouse or civil partner, or
-- src:25 | (iii) a member of a polygamous marriage and is residing with other members of that marriage;
-- src:26 | (b) child benefit would, but for this paragraph, be payable to that person in respect of a child or qualifying young person at the enhanced rate; and
-- src:27 | (c) child benefit would, but for this paragraph, be payable at that rate to one of the other persons listed in paragraphs (i) to (iii) of sub-paragraph (a) in respect of another child or qualifying person,
-- src:28 | the enhanced rate shall be payable in that week in respect of only the elder or eldest of the children and qualifying young persons referred to in sub-paragraphs (b) and (c).
@ref reg 2(2) (src:21-28)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
      `date of birth of the claimant's child` IS A DATE
      `paragraph (2)(b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN   -- child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable to the claimant for the child at the enhanced rate
      others IS A `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` claimant `date of birth of the claimant's child` `paragraph (2)(b) holds` others MEANS
    IF      `paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` claimant                                                                              -- (a)
        AND `paragraph (2)(b) holds`                     -- (b)
        AND others's `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person`   -- (c)
    THEN `the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` `date of birth of the claimant's child` (others's `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children`)
    ELSE JUST TRUE
